_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 91
---
order: 91
---
short_label: X.91
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If an area is contained by a rational straight line and a first apotome, then the side of the area is an apotome.
----
proof:

Let the area {AB} be contained by the rational straight line {AC} and the first apotome {AD}.

I say that the side of the area {AB} is an apotome.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="410" height="190" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.91 diagram" src="propX91.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the area AB (ACBD) on the rational AC and the first
    // apotome AD with its annex DG, bisected at E, F from the application to
    // AG; the parallels EH, FI, GK; and the squares LM (RMPL) and NO (PNXO)
    // about the diameter PR, with the gnomon UVW. Added, all hidden at rest:
    // faceless, strokeless twins AB, AI, FK, DH, EK, DK, AK, LM, NO, MN, LO,
    // ST, and the hexagon UVWg for the gnomon (;0;0;0;0) that carry the
    // highlights, since a raised filled region would cover its neighbours
    // (#140) — the arc owns the name UVW, so captions reach the region with
    // {UVW|UVWg}; transparent segment targets (;0;0;0); solid twins DG, FI,
    // GK (initiallyHidden) so the annex strokes out from D and the parallels
    // down from F and G; a right-angle marker at P for the angle LPM.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, D (line sliders), C (line
    // slider on the perpendicular) — the givens — G and R (line sliders) and
    // the offscreen frees. G arrives with "let DG be its annex" and R with
    // "make the square LM", so both are deferred. B, E, F, H, I, K, M, P, L,
    // N, O, X, S, T, U, V, W are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","C","B","D","ACBD","AB","AC","AD"];
    var ANNEX = GIVEN.concat(["G","DG","AG"]);
