              justifications: [{ claim: "AG, GD rational, commensurable in square only", ref: "X.73" }] },
            { text: "Also, the whole {AG} is commensurable with the rational straight line {AC} set out,",
              visible: ANNEX,
              highlighted: ["AG","AC"] },
            { text: "and the square on {AG} is greater than the square on {GD|DG}",
              visible: ANNEX,
              highlighted: ["AG","DG"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line commensurable in length with {AG}.",
              visible: ANNEX,
              highlighted: ["AG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AD a first apotome", ref: "X.Def.III.1" }] },
            { text: "Therefore if there is applied to {AG} a parallelogram equal to the fourth part of the square on {DG}",
              visible: ANNEX,
              highlighted: ["AG","DG"] },
            { text: "and deficient by a square figure, then it divides it into commensurable parts.",
              visible: ANNEX,
              highlighted: ["AG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "the parts are commensurable", ref: "X.17" }] },
            { text: "Bisect {DG} at {E},",
              visible: BIS,
              highlighted: ["DG","E"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "E", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "apply to {AG} a parallelogram equal to the square on {EG} and deficient by a square figure,",
              visible: BIS,
              highlighted: ["AG","EG"] },
            { text: "and let it be the rectangle {AF} by {FG}.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FG"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "F", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Then {AF} is commensurable with {FG}.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FG"] },
            { text: "Draw {EH}, {FI}, and {GK} through the points {E}, {F}, and {G} parallel to {AC}.",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["EH","FI","GK"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "EH",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "FI",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "GK",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "DFIB", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "IFGK", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Now, since {AF} is commensurable in length with {FG},",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["AF","FG"] },
            { text: "therefore {AG} is also commensurable in length with each of the straight lines {AF} and {FG}.",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["AG","AF","FG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG commensurable with AF, FG", ref: "X.15" }] },
            { text: "But {AG} is commensurable with {AC},",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["AG","AC"] },
            { text: "therefore each of the straight lines {AF} and {FG} is commensurable in length with {AC}.",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["AF","FG","AC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AF, FG commensurable with AC", ref: "X.12" }] },
            { text: "And {AC} is rational, therefore each of the straight lines {AF} and {FG} is also rational,",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["AC","AF","FG"] },
            { text: "so that each of the rectangles {AI} and {FK} is also rational.",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["AI","FK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AI, FK rational", ref: "X.19" }] },
            { text: "Now, since {DE} is commensurable in length with {EG},",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["DE","EG"] },
            { text: "therefore {DG} is also commensurable in length with each of the straight lines {DE} and {EG}.",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["DG","DE","EG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DG commensurable with DE, EG", ref: "X.15" }] },
            { text: "But {DG} is rational and incommensurable in length with {AC},",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["DG","AC"] },
            { text: "therefore each of the straight lines {DE} and {EG} is also rational and incommensurable in length with {AC}.",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["DE","EG","AC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DE, EG incommensurable with AC", ref: "X.13" }] },
            { text: "Therefore each of the rectangles {DH} and {EK} is medial.",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["DH","EK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DH, EK medial", ref: "X.21" }] },
            { text: "Now make the square {LM} equal to {AI},",
              visible: SQ1,
              highlighted: ["LM","AI"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "R",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "RMPL", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and subtract the square {NO} having a common angle with it, the angle {LPM|angP}, and equal to {FK}.",
              visible: SQ2,
              highlighted: ["NO","angP","FK"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "PNXO", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "angP", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Then the squares {LM} and {NO} are about the same diameter.",
              visible: SQ2,
              highlighted: ["LM","NO"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "about the same diameter", ref: "VI.26" }] },
            { text: "Let {PR|RP} be their diameter, and draw the figure.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["RP"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "RP", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "SX", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "TX", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Since the rectangle {AF} by {FG} equals the square on {EG},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FG","EG"] },
            { text: "therefore {AF} is to {EG} as {EG} is to {FG}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","EG","FG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AF : EG = EG : FG", ref: "VI.17" }] },
            { text: "But {AF} is to {EG} as {AI} is to {EK},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","EG","AI","EK"] },
            { text: "and {EG} is to {FG} as {EK} is to {KF|FK},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EG","FG","EK","FK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AF : EG = AI : EK, EG : FG = EK : KF", ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "therefore {EK} is a mean proportional between {AI} and {KF|FK}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EK","AI","FK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AI : EK = EK : KF", ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "But it was proved before that {MN} is also a mean proportional between {LM} and {NO},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MN","LM","NO"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "MN a mean proportional", ref: "X.54's Lemma" }] },
            { text: "and {AI} equals the square {LM}, and {KF|FK} equals {NO}, therefore {MN} also equals {EK}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AI","LM","FK","NO","MN","EK"] },
            { text: "But {EK} equals {DH}, and {MN} equals {LO},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EK","DH","MN","LO"] },
            { text: "therefore {DK} equals the gnomon {UVW|UVWg} and {NO}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DK","UVWg","NO"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "UVWg", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] } },
            { text: "But {AK} also equals the sum of the squares {LM} and {NO},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AK","LM","NO"] },
            { text: "therefore the remainder {AB} equals {ST}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","ST"] },
            { text: "But {ST} is the square on {LN}, therefore the square on {LN} equals {AB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ST","LN","AB"] },
            { text: "Therefore {LN} is the side of {AB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["LN","AB"] },
            { text: "I say next that {LN} is an apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["LN"] },
            { text: "Since each of the rectangles {AI} and {FK} is rational, and they equal {LM} and {NO},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AI","FK","LM","NO"] },
            { text: "therefore each of the squares {LM} and {NO}, that is, the squares on {LP} and {PN} respectively, is also rational.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["LM","NO","LP","PN"] },
            { text: "Therefore each of the straight lines {LP} and {PN} is also rational.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["LP","PN"] },
            { text: "Again, since {DH} is medial and equals {LO}, therefore {LO} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DH","LO"] },
            { text: "Since, then, {LO} is medial, while {NO} is rational, therefore {LO} is incommensurable with {NO}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["LO","NO"] },
            { text: "But {LO} is to {NO} as {LP} is to {PN}, therefore {LP} is incommensurable in length with {PN}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["LO","NO","LP","PN"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "LO : NO = LP : PN", ref: "VI.1" },
                               { claim: "LP, PN incommensurable", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "And both are rational, therefore {LP} and {PN} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["LP","PN"] },
            { text: "Therefore {LN} is an apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["LN"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "LN an apotome", ref: "X.73" }] },
            { text: "And it is the side of the area {AB}, therefore the side of the area {AB} is an apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["LN","AB"] },
            { text: "Therefore, if an area is contained by a rational straight line and a first apotome,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","AC","AD"] },
            { text: "then the side of the area is an apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","LN"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.91") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "V.11":         "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV11/",
        "VI.1":         "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/",
        "VI.17":        "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI17/",
        "VI.26":        "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI26/",
        "X.11":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX11/",
        "X.12":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX12/",
        "X.13":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX13/",
        "X.15":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX15/",
        "X.17":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX17/",
        "X.19":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX19/",
        "X.21":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX21/",
        "X.73":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX73/",
        "X.54's Lemma": "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX54/#lemma",
        "X.Def.III.1":  "/elements/books/bookX/definitions/defX.III.1/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Since {AD} is a first apotome, let {DG} be its annex, therefore {AG} and {GD|DG} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. Also, the whole {AG} is commensurable with the rational straight line {AC} set out, and the square on {AG} is greater than the square on {GD|DG} by the square on a straight line commensurable in length with {AG}. [!just X.73; X.Def.III.1]

Therefore if there is applied to {AG} a parallelogram equal to the fourth part of the square on {DG} and deficient by a square figure, then it divides it into commensurable parts. [!just X.17]

Bisect {DG} at {E}, apply to {AG} a parallelogram equal to the square on {EG} and deficient by a square figure, and let it be the rectangle {AF} by {FG}. Then {AF} is commensurable with {FG}.

Draw {EH}, {FI}, and {GK} through the points {E}, {F}, and {G} parallel to {AC}.

Now, since {AF} is commensurable in length with {FG}, therefore {AG} is also commensurable in length with each of the straight lines {AF} and {FG}. [!just X.15]

But {AG} is commensurable with {AC}, therefore each of the straight lines {AF} and {FG} is commensurable in length with {AC}. [!just X.12]

And {AC} is rational, therefore each of the straight lines {AF} and {FG} is also rational, so that each of the rectangles {AI} and {FK} is also rational. [!just X.19]

Now, since {DE} is commensurable in length with {EG}, therefore {DG} is also commensurable in length with each of the straight lines {DE} and {EG}. [!just X.15]

But {DG} is rational and incommensurable in length with {AC}, therefore each of the straight lines {DE} and {EG} is also rational and incommensurable in length with {AC}. Therefore each of the rectangles {DH} and {EK} is medial. [!just X.13; X.21]

Now make the square {LM} equal to {AI}, and subtract the square {NO} having a common angle with it, the angle {LPM|angP}, and equal to {FK}. Then the squares {LM} and {NO} are about the same diameter. [!just VI.26]

Let {PR|RP} be their diameter, and draw the figure.

Since the rectangle {AF} by {FG} equals the square on {EG}, therefore {AF} is to {EG} as {EG} is to {FG}. [!just VI.17]

But {AF} is to {EG} as {AI} is to {EK}, and {EG} is to {FG} as {EK} is to {KF|FK}, therefore {EK} is a mean proportional between {AI} and {KF|FK}. [!just VI.1; V.11]

But it was proved before that {MN} is also a mean proportional between {LM} and {NO}, and {AI} equals the square {LM}, and {KF|FK} equals {NO}, therefore {MN} also equals {EK}. <div class="just"><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX54/#lemma">X.54's Lemma</a></div>

But {EK} equals {DH}, and {MN} equals {LO}, therefore {DK} equals the gnomon {UVW|UVWg} and {NO}.

But {AK} also equals the sum of the squares {LM} and {NO}, therefore the remainder {AB} equals {ST}.

But {ST} is the square on {LN}, therefore the square on {LN} equals {AB}. Therefore {LN} is the side of {AB}.

I say next that {LN} is an apotome.

Since each of the rectangles {AI} and {FK} is rational, and they equal {LM} and {NO}, therefore each of the squares {LM} and {NO}, that is, the squares on {LP} and {PN} respectively, is also rational. Therefore each of the straight lines {LP} and {PN} is also rational.

Again, since {DH} is medial and equals {LO}, therefore {LO} is also medial.

Since, then, {LO} is medial, while {NO} is rational, therefore {LO} is incommensurable with {NO}.

But {LO} is to {NO} as {LP} is to {PN}, therefore {LP} is incommensurable in length with {PN}. [!just VI.1, X.11]

And both are rational, therefore {LP} and {PN} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. Therefore {LN} is an apotome. [!just X.73]

And it is the side of the area {AB}, therefore the side of the area {AB} is an apotome.

Therefore, *if an area is contained by a rational straight line and a first apotome, then the side of the area is an apotome.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
